artifact.self_contained_problem:
In the Standard Model description of weak decays of charmed hadrons, the inclusive semileptonic width Γ_SL(H_c) = Σ_X Γ(H_c → X ℓ ν_ℓ) of a charm hadron H_c (summed over all hadronic final states X and over light charged leptons ℓ = e, μ) and the corresponding inclusive semileptonic branching ratio B_SL(H_c) = Γ_SL(H_c)/Γ_tot(H_c) encode the interplay between spectator quark dynamics and nonspectator effects such as weak annihilation (WA), Pauli interference, and W-exchange. Determine experimentally, with an accuracy of at least 5% on the widths:

(a) the inclusive semileptonic branching ratios B(D_s → ℓ X), B(Λ_c → ℓ X), B(Ξ_c^0 → ℓ X), and B(Ξ_c^+ → ℓ X);

(b) the corresponding total semileptonic widths Γ_SL of D_s, Λ_c, Ξ_c^0, and Ξ_c^+;

(c) the charged-lepton energy spectra dΓ_SL/dE_ℓ of these hadrons.

The goal is to compare these quantities among themselves and against the corresponding nonleptonic widths in order to quantify the size of weak annihilation contributions and to calibrate the inclusive heavy-flavor decay dynamics governing charm hadrons.

